# MAMA CARE — environment variables live with the part that reads them.
#
#   web/.env.example        → everything the browser may know (public values only)
#   functions/.env.example  → everything secret (Cloudinary API secret, Admin SDK
#                             credentials, SMS provider keys, email relay)
#
# Copy the one you need, e.g.
#
#   cp web/.env.example web/.env.local
#   cp functions/.env.example functions/.env
#
# Both `.env` files are git-ignored. Never commit a real value, never paste a service
# account JSON or an API secret into a chat or an issue, and never put a secret behind a
# `VITE_` prefix: Vite inlines those into the browser bundle.
#
# With nothing configured, the app runs against this browser's IndexedDB using the same
# policy module, validation, alert engine and reporting code as the hosted build. Missing
# credentials are reported by name in the interface; nothing is faked.
